From d29f760577ea8217eefee5e030ce0a845096b406 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cindy Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:59:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stats: leave pairs with insert size 0 out of the insert size
 statistics

A TLEN of 0 means the insert size is unknown (SAM spec: "set as 0 for a
single-segment template or when the information is unavailable").  The
insert size average and standard deviation nevertheless counted such
pairs in their denominator, the standard deviation added them to the
denominator but not to the sum of squares, and the -m main-bulk cut-off
counted them towards its percentile, so a file dominated by TLEN 0 pairs
reported an average of 0.  They are now left out of all three; the IS
rows still list them.  On the new test input (10 pairs, two with TLEN 0,
the rest 300 to 360) the average is 323.8 and the SD 18.0, the values
for the eight pairs with a known insert size (previously 259.0 and
60.1); with -m 0.65 the cut-off now falls after six of those eight
pairs, average 315.0 and SD 9.6 (previously 222.9 and 75.6).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
---
 NEWS.md                     |  6 ++++++
 stats.c                     |  8 +++++++-
 test/stat/23.stats.expected |  2 ++
 test/stat/23_isize_zero.sam | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 test/stat/24.stats.expected |  2 ++
 test/test.pl                |  4 ++++
 6 files changed, 43 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 test/stat/23.stats.expected
 create mode 100644 test/stat/23_isize_zero.sam
 create mode 100644 test/stat/24.stats.expected

diff --git a/NEWS.md b/NEWS.md
index 016ee0b..aafa48b 100644
--- a/NEWS.md
+++ b/NEWS.md
@@ -34,6 +34,12 @@ Bug fixes:
   had flagged the supplementary records of duplicates.  Duplicates are now
   counted for the same records as `sequences`.
 
+* FIX.  `samtools stats` counted pairs with insert size 0 (TLEN unknown) in
+  the denominator of `insert size average` and `insert size standard
+  deviation`, and in the mean but not in the sum of squares of the standard
+  deviation.  They are now left out of both statistics and of the `-m`
+  main-bulk cut-off.
+
 Release 1.24 (9th July 2026)
 ----------------------------
 
diff --git a/stats.c b/stats.c
index c69e558..fc25e08 100644
--- a/stats.c
+++ b/stats.c
@@ -1584,7 +1584,13 @@ void output_stats(FILE *to, stats_t *stats, int sparse)
         nisize += stats->isize->inward(stats->isize->data, isize) + stats->isize->outward(stats->isize->data, isize) + stats->isize->other(stats->isize->data, isize);
     }
 
-    for (isize=0; isize<stats->isize->nitems(stats->isize->data); isize++)
+    // Pairs with isize 0 (TLEN unknown) are left out of the main-bulk
+    // cut-off, the average and the standard deviation, from the numerator and
+    // the denominator alike.  The IS rows below still list them.
+    uint64_t nisize_zero = stats->isize->inward(stats->isize->data, 0) + stats->isize->outward(stats->isize->data, 0) + stats->isize->other(stats->isize->data, 0);
+    nisize = nisize > nisize_zero ? nisize - nisize_zero : 0;
+    if (nisize_zero > 0) ibulk = 1;
+    for (isize=1; isize<stats->isize->nitems(stats->isize->data); isize++)
     {
         uint64_t num = stats->isize->inward(stats->isize->data, isize) +  stats->isize->outward(stats->isize->data, isize) + stats->isize->other(stats->isize->data, isize);
         if (num > 0) ibulk = isize + 1;
